WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.933
Your agent already did the thinking.

00:01.933 --> 00:05.153
Give that work a format people actually want to explore.

00:05.153 --> 00:07.086
Meet Publish HTML.

00:08.486 --> 00:10.705
Start with analysis you already have.

00:10.705 --> 00:15.884
For this demo, we used TauLang, a Go interpreter with Hindi English keywords.

00:15.884 --> 00:18.473
The skill handles the presentation and publishing.

00:19.873 --> 00:24.616
Instead of a wall of text, the result is a focused, interactive field guide.

00:24.616 --> 00:28.682
A clear introduction, a system map, and a trace you can follow.

00:30.082 --> 00:31.513
Click through the pipeline.

00:31.513 --> 00:35.806
See the source become tokens, then a syntax tree, then a value.

00:35.806 --> 00:39.025
These outputs were captured from the real Go interpreter.

00:39.025 --> 00:41.887
This is an explanation, not a browser runtime.

00:43.287 --> 00:46.293
Switch from a binding to a function or an array.

00:46.293 --> 00:51.103
The views stay in sync, so the relationship between code and result becomes easier to see.

00:52.503 --> 00:56.025
A system map explains the responsibilities at a glance.

00:56.025 --> 00:59.547
A searchable vocabulary connects unfamiliar keywords to familiar ideas.

00:59.547 --> 01:01.503
Every component has a job.

01:01.503 --> 01:03.460
There is no widget quota.

01:04.860 --> 01:11.024
The publisher reuses your GitHub Pages repository, uploads the page, and verifies the live files.

01:11.024 --> 01:16.366
Revisions keep the same document URL, with previous versions retained in Git history.

01:17.766 --> 01:18.517
Want feedback?

01:18.517 --> 01:20.771
Enable optional page comments with Giscus.

01:20.771 --> 01:25.653
Your agent can read the discussion and reply, then publish the next revision.

01:25.653 --> 01:28.658
Reading the page never requires a GitHub login.

01:30.058 --> 01:32.289
Reports, system explanations, dashboards, and more.

01:32.289 --> 01:37.493
Bring your content, ask for Publish HTML, and get a link.

01:37.493 --> 01:41.211
Clone the skill and try it with your next explanation.
